# Decrypted secrets.
#
# The SOPS round-trip documented in SERVER_CONFIG.md writes the plaintext right next
# to the encrypted file (`sops -d secrets.enc.yaml > secrets.yaml`), so the plaintext
# form has to be unstageable from anywhere in the tree -- not just from one app.
#
# A pattern that contains a slash is anchored to the directory holding this file,
# which is why the previous `sonarqube/secrets.yaml` rule matched nothing at all:
# the app lives in apps/sonarqube/, so only a top-level sonarqube/ was ever covered.
# The rules below carry no slash, so git applies them at every level.
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.dec.yaml
*.decrypted.yaml

# ...but never the encrypted form: those are committed on purpose, and Flux decrypts
# them at apply time. Kept explicit so a broader rule added above cannot swallow them.
!*.enc.yaml

# age / SOPS private keys
*.agekey
age-key.txt
age.agekey
keys.txt

# Cluster credentials and private key material
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
k3s.yaml
*.pem
*.key
